From 66ca5a58ce31cb557fd60c33b0424bdf400eb0f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:46:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 07/42] Add LivenessPage and LivenessController per the shared
 UI spec

lib/ui/liveness/ (docs/ui-liveness-spec.md in Mosip26):
- liveness_controller.dart: a ChangeNotifier without widgets that turns the
  event and result maps into an immutable LivenessViewState (phase, status /
  hint / challenge / message / recovery keys, step i of n, progress or
  indeterminate, attempt a of m, retries left, oval tone + icon,
  Retry / Cancel / Close, tips). Rules from spec sections 3 and 4:
  guidance shown at once, or after the rest of 500 ms since the last one
  (latest wins), cleared and dropped by CHECKING_PASSIVE, CHALLENGE_PROMPT,
  CHALLENGE_PROGRESS ("Please continue"), PASSED and failures;
  LOOK_AT_CAMERA after ACTION_DETECTED / HOLD_STILL; errors only through
  the user message (PAD and engine errors: the generic text, no tips; tips
  only for LIVENESS_NOT_VERIFIED); FAILED_FINAL always max_attempts_reached
  or the device text, plus liveness.recovery.<workflow>, Close only, which
  also covers the cooldown refusal; camera permission refused: the device
  text, recovery and Close. Timers come from an injectable factory.
- liveness_strings.dart: the one switch from canonical keys to the
  generated AppLocalizations getters, with the placeholders.
- liveness_page.dart: LivenessPage(workflow, camera, useFake,
  previewBuilder, service, showDebugInfo) pops a LivenessOutcome (passed,
  cancelled, disabled, passPath, failureCode, userMessage, bestFrameJpeg,
  sessionId, attempts, durationMs, modelVersion). Flow: isEnabled (else
  pop disabled), camera permission, policy (m = maxRetries + 1), wait for
  the platform view, startSession. Layout per spec section 2: the 3:4
  preview (AndroidView or previewBuilder) with a face oval in the tone
  colour, a light dim outside it and an icon badge; the status line in a
  26 sp banner inside Semantics(liveRegion); the hint (18 sp, warning icon
  for guidance); step and progress bar; attempt line; tips; recovery text;
  48 dp buttons. PASSED: success state, then pop after 1 s. Back and Cancel
  cancel the session; dispose() cancels a running one. A result of an
  older session is ignored. No score or model information on screen; in
  debug builds only, a small chip with the model version.
- LivenessService gets ensureCameraPermission(); startSession uses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
